 is C$5.1B, about 1.2 times the revenue guide, which supports the guidance. I couldn't find a 2026 revenue figure, so there is no growth rate.\n2. **Tarnwell Electric (TRNW):** Revenue is expected to grow about 6% and operating margin to rise to 14% from 12%. Price increases drive both, so the two figures don't confirm each other. If the increases don't hold, both would fall short.\n3. **Braxen Cable (BRXC):** Revenue should rise about 2%, all from pass-through pricing, because volumes are flat. Copper costs are up 18%, which squeezes margins, and earnings are expected to be flat. The documents give no dollar or margin figures. Pricing mostly offsetting copper is my inference, not something the documents state.\n4. **Ostrand Meters (OSTM):** The Norvane Utilities smart-meter contract adds about 20% to 2027 revenue. Margins dip one point as the rollout ramps, and the dip may ease as it matures. The source doesn't say whether the margin is gross or operating, and it gives no dollar figures.\n5. **Kelby Switchgear (KLBS):** Revenue is expected to fall about 5% as Kelby loses medium-voltage share to Tarnwell. Operating margin should hold near 8%, supported by restructuring. The sources don't say whether 8% is flat on 2026. The 5% decline is a point estimate with no range.\n\nOf the five, Ostrand has the strongest revenue growth and Kelby is the only one expected to shrink.","ttft_ms":3239,"type":"result","duration_ms":47007,"uuid":"21cd1e25-85cd-45dc-b76a-3ae579190aa3","ttft_stream_ms":2345,"time_to_request_ms":1142,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":85,"system_prompt":57,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":89,"input_attachments":200,"input_hooks":25,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":230,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":111,"init_frame_send":29,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":33,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":62,"request_announcements":113,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":19,"message_normalization":25,"client_cr